WEBVTT

00:10.760 --> 00:12.095
<i>What you wanna be?</i>

00:16.016 --> 00:17.642
<i>We are the frontiers</i>

00:21.062 --> 00:22.814
<i>Confront with no fear</i>

00:22.897 --> 00:24.983
<i>From zero to a hundred in an instant</i>

00:25.066 --> 00:27.652
<i>Unveiling mysteries hidden</i>
<i>deep in the dark</i>

00:28.236 --> 00:30.113
<i>Even dead, I rise from the dust</i>

00:30.196 --> 00:32.741
<i>Reaching an unprecedented realm</i>

00:32.824 --> 00:35.035
<i>Trying your uniqueness</i>

00:35.118 --> 00:36.286
<i>It's a test level EX</i>

00:36.369 --> 00:37.662
<i>I'm the best, nothing less</i>

00:37.746 --> 00:40.206
<i>Pioneering from the east to the west</i>

00:40.290 --> 00:42.917
<i>Erasing all who resist, their data and all</i>

00:43.001 --> 00:44.210
<i>Did I really win?</i>

00:44.294 --> 00:45.503
<i>What are these tears?</i>

00:45.587 --> 00:47.922
<i>Who will be hated or loved</i>
<i>by the god of victory?</i>

00:48.006 --> 00:49.215
<i>To Each, their own wishes</i>

00:49.299 --> 00:50.300
<i>With friends, aiming for prize</i>

00:50.383 --> 00:52.343
<i>Seeking answers,</i>
<i>cutting through the unknown</i>

00:52.427 --> 00:53.678
<i>What you wanna be?</i>

00:53.762 --> 00:56.097
<i>Bugged out world, I'm a survivor</i>

00:56.181 --> 00:58.475
<i>Blazing with the guiding fire</i>

00:58.558 --> 01:00.310
<i>Show me the Show me the Shangri-La</i>

01:00.393 --> 01:01.436
<i>What you wanna be?</i>

01:01.519 --> 01:02.812
<i>Show me the Show me the Shangri-La</i>

01:02.896 --> 01:03.730
<i>What you wanna be?</i>

01:03.813 --> 01:06.691
<i>Declare war. At the system, we aim back</i>

01:06.775 --> 01:09.069
<i>Lose yourself, and it's game over</i>

01:09.152 --> 01:10.987
<i>Show me the Show me the Shangri-La</i>

01:11.071 --> 01:11.905
<i>What you wanna be?</i>

01:11.988 --> 01:13.281
<i>Show me the Show me the Shangri-La</i>

01:13.364 --> 01:14.699
<i>What you wanna be?</i>

01:18.703 --> 01:20.121
<i>We are the frontiers</i>

01:23.833 --> 01:25.335
<i>Confront with no fear</i>

01:26.252 --> 01:27.462
<i>You know I'll be there</i>

01:27.545 --> 01:28.713
<i>Overturning limits</i>

01:28.797 --> 01:30.507
<i>Now is the new beginning</i>

01:31.466 --> 01:32.801
Along with my Moonblades,

01:32.884 --> 01:36.429
I've also had my Marsh Daggers
reforged through evolving.

01:36.513 --> 01:38.014
Now Ducusram!

01:38.097 --> 01:39.933
Time for your debut!

01:40.016 --> 01:41.434
Let's go!

01:42.185 --> 01:45.772
(End of Tranquility,
Dawn of the Ruined City)

01:52.195 --> 01:53.029
Rust!

01:53.113 --> 01:55.865
We will stop the ones on the right,
you deal with the ones on the left!

01:55.949 --> 01:56.783
Got it!

01:58.243 --> 01:59.119
Let's do this!

01:59.202 --> 02:00.912
Y-Yessir!

02:00.995 --> 02:02.997
Magic Edge!

02:06.960 --> 02:09.921
<i>Marsh Daggers' main</i>
<i>selling point is its toughness.</i>

02:10.004 --> 02:11.381
<i>But instead of the usual upgrade,</i>

02:11.464 --> 02:15.718
<i>I had Beelach evolve them</i>
<i>to improve on their vitality.</i>

02:16.719 --> 02:22.142
<i>They are now a pair of one-handed swords</i>
<i>just as powerful as those wielded by a hero.</i>

02:26.062 --> 02:29.065
Here we go, Ducusram!

02:31.442 --> 02:33.236
Unbroken Lightdance!

02:36.239 --> 02:42.579
<i>They're not just tough, they can also negate</i>
<i>the durability loss after a critical hit.</i>

02:42.662 --> 02:45.665
With this thing,
I can endure long battles!

02:49.294 --> 02:52.797
Well, with you as my opponent…

02:52.881 --> 02:55.174
…I doubt it will…

02:55.258 --> 02:57.010
….take that much time!

03:03.308 --> 03:05.685
<i>Still, something feels weird.</i>

03:06.311 --> 03:10.690
<i>Isn't this a little too easy for</i>
<i>a boss fight in a Unique Scenario?</i>

03:11.441 --> 03:13.109
<i>Or maybe…</i>

03:13.192 --> 03:16.404
<i>There's a stronger boss</i>
<i>waiting to make their entrance?</i>

03:16.487 --> 03:17.488
<i>It's possible. </i>

03:17.572 --> 03:21.993
<i>But you can say it's our party size</i>
<i>that makes this fishman horde manageable.</i>

03:22.076 --> 03:25.121
<i>Maybe this is just how it</i>
<i>is when you don't solo it?</i>

03:25.872 --> 03:27.540
You damned monster!

03:29.167 --> 03:31.711
I will avenge my dad!

03:32.962 --> 03:34.005
Stude?

03:34.088 --> 03:36.507
Huh? Why are you here?

03:36.591 --> 03:39.969
Didn't you say you will leave
the fighting to us?

03:40.053 --> 03:43.348
I can fight too, you know!

03:43.431 --> 03:45.850
Huh? What are you saying?

03:48.895 --> 03:51.064
He's ignoring us and
running straight to Stude?!

03:52.857 --> 03:54.651
So that's what this is!

03:54.734 --> 03:56.819
This is not a simple subjugation mission!

03:56.903 --> 03:59.697
This is an escort mission! Protect Stude!

03:59.781 --> 04:01.074
An escort mission?!

04:01.157 --> 04:02.408
And we must protect Stude?

04:02.492 --> 04:04.869
This is not just a horde battle!

04:05.912 --> 04:07.705
I won't make it!

04:20.426 --> 04:23.638
My stats debuff don't make things easy,

04:23.721 --> 04:27.600
but with this equipment set,
I should be able to fight well enough!

04:28.768 --> 04:31.062
What? Is that…

04:31.145 --> 04:32.438
Who?

04:32.522 --> 04:34.816
Rei, is that you?

04:35.775 --> 04:39.404
I thought we were dealing with
a new monster for a moment.

04:39.487 --> 04:40.947
You saved us, Rei!

04:41.030 --> 04:42.824
Babysit Stude for us!

04:42.907 --> 04:44.325
B-Babysit?!

04:44.409 --> 04:46.828
I said I'm fighting with yo-

04:52.792 --> 04:54.544
I'm on it!

04:55.503 --> 04:58.047
Emul! Mordo! Rust!

04:58.131 --> 05:00.675
The enemy's fully focused on Stude!

05:00.758 --> 05:02.218
Stay focused!

05:02.302 --> 05:04.679
- Yes!
- Got it! - Roger!

05:04.762 --> 05:07.432
If this is an escort mission,

05:07.515 --> 05:09.934
we can't afford to waste our time!

05:10.018 --> 05:12.603
Let's put an end to this right away!

05:14.480 --> 05:16.190
I'm sorry!

05:16.274 --> 05:19.527
We're late! We will
join the fight here now!

05:33.583 --> 05:35.209
<i>That sensation just now…</i>

05:35.835 --> 05:38.004
<i>It felt like the time just</i>
<i>stopped for a moment.</i>

05:42.091 --> 05:43.509
<i>A lag?</i>

05:43.593 --> 05:48.097
<i>It's like that moment of jitter you get</i>
<i>when a game's loading a lot of data.</i>

05:48.765 --> 05:54.479
<i>But I've never experienced</i>
<i>a lag playing</i> SLF <i>so far.</i>

05:54.562 --> 05:57.982
<i>Not even when I face that</i>
<i>massive Overdress Golem.</i>

06:00.902 --> 06:03.571
Stude! You stay back for now!

06:09.202 --> 06:11.579
The storm is getting fiercer,
'twould seem!

06:17.293 --> 06:20.129
Oh crap, oh crap, we're gonna fall!

06:23.800 --> 06:26.385
We can't fight in this!

06:26.469 --> 06:29.764
Yeah, all we can do is to hang on.

06:43.111 --> 06:45.571
This is bad! This is bad!

06:45.655 --> 06:48.241
A huge tentacle that
could grab an island!

06:48.324 --> 06:51.327
Sunraku-san, this… this is…

06:51.410 --> 06:54.455
Ctarnidd!

06:56.666 --> 06:59.168
What did you say?!

07:08.636 --> 07:12.140
Ctarnidd of the Abyss…

07:19.230 --> 07:22.275
We're still in the middle of
a regular Unique Scenario.

07:22.358 --> 07:24.569
So why are we seeing
a Unique Monster already!?

07:24.652 --> 07:25.778
Are we fighting it like this?

07:25.862 --> 07:30.283
You're kidding me.
This scenario goes straight to EX?

07:30.366 --> 07:35.413
Wait, wait! Don't there usually be
a warning for this before we start?!

07:37.915 --> 07:40.126
(EX Unique Scenario
Behold the Abyss Above, As the World Turns on Its Head
Begins)

07:42.378 --> 07:43.963
Don't…

07:44.046 --> 07:48.843
Don't tell us <i>after</i> the fact, you bastard!

07:57.226 --> 07:58.769
The seabed…

08:03.566 --> 08:04.942
Huh?

08:08.488 --> 08:11.574
A forced knock-out? That's rare.

08:12.158 --> 08:13.701
What's going on?

08:16.204 --> 08:21.209
Hey, Emul! Everyone, where are you?!

08:25.087 --> 08:30.885
<i>No enemies, no party members,</i>
<i>not even Ctarnidd.</i>

08:30.968 --> 08:33.221
<i>This ain't about escorting</i>
<i>Stude any longer.</i>

08:33.304 --> 08:36.390
<i>This is bad. I never saw this coming.</i>

08:37.850 --> 08:44.774
<i>Who would've thought this lead</i>
<i>directly to a likely lethal EX scenario?</i>

08:44.857 --> 08:48.277
<i>It was a bad idea to bring Emul along.</i>

08:48.361 --> 08:50.696
Besides, where the hell am I?

08:50.780 --> 08:53.866
Did I get dragged into
a seabed cave or somethi-

08:54.408 --> 08:57.912
No, if anything, this is…

08:57.995 --> 08:59.914
A seabed city.

08:59.997 --> 09:03.251
(The Abyssal Capital Ruluiath)

09:09.966 --> 09:12.176
What's going on here?

09:13.719 --> 09:15.221
For now…

09:16.138 --> 09:19.392
I get to meet the "Master of the Abyss"
earlier than expected.

09:19.475 --> 09:20.726
That's fine and all.

09:20.810 --> 09:23.521
It was kind of a rough invitation,
but I'll let it slide.

09:24.605 --> 09:25.898
But…

09:26.816 --> 09:28.651
Ctarnidd of the Abyss.

09:29.277 --> 09:32.363
What a heck of a monster
the devs created for us.

09:32.446 --> 09:34.699
They want us to go
toe-to-toe with <i>that</i> thing?!

09:35.449 --> 09:38.035
Heh, now that's fun.

09:38.119 --> 09:40.496
Seven Colossi!

09:40.580 --> 09:45.084
But before that, I gotta find the others.

09:45.167 --> 09:50.214
Where are you, Emul?!

09:55.636 --> 09:58.723
That voice just now…
There's someone nearby.

09:59.724 --> 10:01.267
But who?

10:05.021 --> 10:07.023
(Deep Abyss Moray)

10:07.106 --> 10:11.611
<i>Are these the zombie fishmen from before?</i>

10:12.653 --> 10:14.780
<i>Now they're just items.</i>

10:15.573 --> 10:17.908
<i>Can I put them into my Inventoria?</i>

10:19.118 --> 10:20.620
<i>Oh, I can.</i>

10:21.162 --> 10:23.581
Not really sure why, but for now…

10:24.123 --> 10:26.917
I'd like some info on this seabed city.

10:28.586 --> 10:31.964
A city covered in a light shade of blue.

10:33.132 --> 10:35.635
And a castle in the center of it.

10:36.260 --> 10:39.180
If Ctarnidd's around, it's gotta be there.

10:40.598 --> 10:46.562
And this EX Unique Scenario
that started in the middle of battle.

10:46.646 --> 10:50.900
"Behold the abyss above,
as the world turns on its head."

10:51.901 --> 10:55.946
That lag-like thing that occurred
right before this scenario began.

10:56.030 --> 11:01.285
It occurred the moment Akitsuakane
hopped over to the ghost ship.

11:02.119 --> 11:04.872
The requirements were Stude being alive,

11:04.955 --> 11:10.586
and all party members boarding
the ghost ship Crying Innsman…

11:10.670 --> 11:11.921
I suppose?

11:13.297 --> 11:16.092
<i>What's this? A countdown?</i>

11:16.175 --> 11:17.676
<i>Unique Condition…</i>

11:18.469 --> 11:22.264
<i>The Guiding Torch</i>
<i>I got from fighting Lycagon</i>

11:22.348 --> 11:24.850
<i>was also a Unique Condition,</i>
<i>if I remember correctly.</i>

11:24.934 --> 11:28.354
<i>If this is part of an EX Unique</i>
<i>Scenario's special gimmick,</i>

11:28.437 --> 11:31.232
<i>then Wethermon's level</i>
<i>restriction could also be that.</i>

11:31.941 --> 11:34.652
<i>This time it's a ticking clock.</i>

11:34.735 --> 11:39.281
<i>In other words, the "Master</i>
<i>of the Abyss" invited me here,</i>

11:39.365 --> 11:43.452
<i>and telling me I have</i>
<i>170 hours or seven days</i>

11:43.536 --> 11:46.872
<i>to conquer this seabed city,</i>
<i>the lair of Ctarnidd of the Abyss.</i>

11:46.956 --> 11:49.875
<i>I don't know if that's</i>
<i>a lot of time or not,</i>

11:49.959 --> 11:52.628
<i>but if I have seven days for this,</i>
<i>they should allow me to log out.</i>

11:52.711 --> 11:57.967
<i>Is there a safe zone or</i>
<i>a place I can respawn at?</i>

11:59.593 --> 12:02.388
<i>All the houses have been boarded up.</i>

12:02.471 --> 12:04.849
<i>And from the outside, nonetheless.</i>

12:04.932 --> 12:07.977
<i>Were they keeping the</i>
<i>residents from going outside?</i>

12:09.437 --> 12:11.689
<i>I have a bad feeling about this.</i>

12:12.356 --> 12:15.484
<i>I should hurry up and</i>
<i>meet up with the rest.</i>

12:15.568 --> 12:17.445
<i>Especially with NPCs like Emul.</i>

12:17.528 --> 12:21.323
<i>Once they get beaten,</i>
<i>there's no taking that back.</i>

12:21.407 --> 12:23.033
Hey!

12:23.117 --> 12:24.952
Anybody here?!

12:25.035 --> 12:26.620
Emul!

12:27.288 --> 12:29.540
<i>In the end, without any info,</i>

12:29.623 --> 12:33.169
<i>all I can do is explore while</i>
<i>looking for my party members.</i>

12:33.252 --> 12:35.129
Emul!

12:37.548 --> 12:39.091
<i>Was that a person?</i>

12:39.175 --> 12:41.051
<i>A monster?</i>

12:41.135 --> 12:42.136
<i>Rei?</i>

12:42.761 --> 12:43.971
<i>No.</i>

12:44.638 --> 12:47.725
<i>Is that a tail? So it is a monster?</i>

12:48.893 --> 12:49.894
Huh?

12:55.316 --> 12:57.318
A-A school of fish?!

12:57.401 --> 12:59.570
They even show up here?!

13:00.446 --> 13:03.824
What's up with this horde?
There are too many of them!

13:03.908 --> 13:06.785
Not only that, they got better equipment
than the ones on the ghost ship!

13:07.536 --> 13:09.330
Mirror of Fading!

13:09.413 --> 13:11.373
Have fun with my afterimage!

13:12.416 --> 13:13.918
Damn it, it didn't work!

13:14.001 --> 13:17.087
With their number,
it won't distract them for long.

13:17.171 --> 13:19.381
But they seem dumb.

13:19.465 --> 13:22.426
None of them left the crowd
to try cutting me off.

13:22.510 --> 13:25.721
You guys won't have any luck
capturing me like that!

13:26.388 --> 13:27.890
Shana-oh Possession!

13:27.973 --> 13:30.392
Gravity Zero Lv.1!

13:30.476 --> 13:31.477
Activate!

13:36.106 --> 13:38.609
Without the brain to do things
other than charging ahead,

13:38.692 --> 13:41.737
they're bound to be stuck
to the wall like a clump.

13:41.820 --> 13:45.282
They'd make some big fish sticks.
Rotten ones, that is.

13:46.242 --> 13:49.161
Still, where are there so many of them?

13:49.245 --> 13:51.372
They remind me of <i>that</i>.

13:52.540 --> 13:55.292
<i>A VR game with the a sales pitch;</i>

13:55.376 --> 13:59.922
<i>"Experience an overwhelming despair</i>
<i>with your whole body,"</i> Cosmo Buster.

14:00.005 --> 14:03.050
<i>The stage 5 was particularly awful.</i>

14:03.133 --> 14:05.469
<i>To help the federation</i>
<i>ally forces retreat,</i>

14:05.553 --> 14:09.265
<i>the player was forced to face</i>
<i>the military all by themselves.</i>

14:09.890 --> 14:12.810
<i>After many trials and errors,</i>
<i>the solution I found was…</i>

14:12.893 --> 14:17.815
<i>…to use a bug to sprint up a wall</i>
<i>and keep running away.</i>

14:17.898 --> 14:20.317
Sometimes <i>not</i> fighting
is the right answer.

14:20.401 --> 14:23.028
I sure learned that the hard way.

14:24.113 --> 14:28.742
Memory is experience and
experience is power, as they say.

14:30.160 --> 14:31.579
When were you there?!

14:31.662 --> 14:32.997
There are some up here, too?!

14:33.080 --> 14:35.332
W-Wait, Birdian!

14:35.416 --> 14:37.042
- I'm not one of them!
- He talks?!

14:37.877 --> 14:40.379
<i>Is this the guy I saw running earlier?</i>

14:40.462 --> 14:44.383
<i>Yeah, he does look different from those</i>
<i>rotting brain-dead fish sticks down there.</i>

14:44.466 --> 14:46.176
<i>Is he an event-related NPC?</i>

14:47.052 --> 14:48.679
That wound…

14:49.430 --> 14:51.348
Are you being chased by those guys?

14:56.437 --> 14:58.689
They actually climbed right up?!

14:59.273 --> 15:02.735
A mob where nobody has
free will is a scary thing.

15:02.818 --> 15:03.903
Damn them!

15:08.198 --> 15:09.491
Here.

15:11.118 --> 15:13.787
I-Is this a healing potion?

15:13.871 --> 15:15.372
Drink that and run!

15:17.499 --> 15:18.584
We're out of here.

15:18.667 --> 15:20.419
O-Okay.

15:23.130 --> 15:25.507
I don't know who you are,
but thank you!

15:25.591 --> 15:27.259
Don't mind it!

15:28.844 --> 15:34.183
<i>I didn't expect to meet an NPC</i>
<i>before other players.</i>

15:35.351 --> 15:37.937
<i>But this is clearly an event flag.</i>

15:38.020 --> 15:40.606
<i>And there's no way I'd let that go!</i>

15:41.440 --> 15:46.236
<i>And I might get some information</i>
<i>about this area from this guy.</i>

15:47.738 --> 15:50.991
<i>Something that can lead me</i>
<i>to find Emul and the others!</i>

15:51.575 --> 15:54.912
Your voice. You were the one
who shouted earlier, weren't you?

15:54.995 --> 15:55.913
What?

15:55.996 --> 15:59.917
A word of advice; don't make
much noise for no reason.

16:00.000 --> 16:03.963
They mostly rely on their eyes
and ears to seek out enemies.

16:04.046 --> 16:07.424
If you aren't careful,
they'll gang up like that!

16:07.508 --> 16:10.761
Huh? Did I get you that wound, then?

16:10.844 --> 16:13.097
Don't mind it. It was my mistake.

16:13.681 --> 16:17.351
Anyway, I'd like to talk with you.

16:18.602 --> 16:20.020
I'm Araba.

16:20.104 --> 16:21.230
Araba!

16:21.313 --> 16:23.649
I've never seen you before,
but I'll return the favor.

16:23.732 --> 16:26.318
But first, let's find somewhere safe.

16:26.402 --> 16:27.903
Roger!

16:27.987 --> 16:30.239
I'm Sunraku. Nice to meet you.

16:30.322 --> 16:33.993
Also, I'm not a Birdian.
I'm a regular human.

16:34.076 --> 16:35.327
This is just a mask.

16:35.411 --> 16:37.830
What? You go around like <i>that</i>?

16:38.497 --> 16:40.249
You <i>are</i> featherless for one, yeah.

16:55.889 --> 16:58.976
We lost the zombie fishmen for now.

16:59.059 --> 17:03.605
Though, you're one of them, right?
Why are they after you too?

17:03.689 --> 17:05.357
"One of them," you say?

17:05.441 --> 17:07.568
I am a proud Merman!

17:08.235 --> 17:10.988
Don't confuse me with
those poor imitations.

17:11.071 --> 17:14.533
It's like me comparing you
to a wild bird!

17:14.616 --> 17:17.953
Like I said, I'm not
a "Birdian" or whatever.

17:18.787 --> 17:22.750
<i>Seems like any building we can gain</i>
<i>access to can serve as a Save Zone</i>

17:22.833 --> 17:26.336
<i>as long as we've fully</i>
<i>fled from the enemy.</i>

17:27.421 --> 17:30.591
<i>Well, I'm gonna be exploring</i>
<i>this large city for seven days.</i>

17:30.674 --> 17:33.010
<i>It'd be bad if I can't do that much.</i>

17:34.136 --> 17:36.013
<i>Save complete.</i>

17:36.096 --> 17:39.349
Well, I got a lot I wanna ask you,

17:39.433 --> 17:42.352
but well, let's start with this city-

17:42.436 --> 17:43.729
- Wait.
- Huh?

17:45.856 --> 17:47.399
I hear a song.

17:48.108 --> 17:50.194
Oh no! It's the mermaids!

17:51.528 --> 17:52.696
Mermaids?

17:55.491 --> 17:58.577
Whoa!
Those mermaids are flying in the sky!

17:58.660 --> 18:00.037
Let's go check them out real quick.

18:00.120 --> 18:01.789
What are you saying!

18:01.872 --> 18:04.666
They got us by surprise!
We have to leave here now-

18:08.295 --> 18:09.546
Araba?

18:09.630 --> 18:14.510
The human-like top… is a trap…!

18:16.136 --> 18:18.680
To get their target lower their guard!

18:18.764 --> 18:19.765
It's a disguise!

18:20.390 --> 18:22.935
Once they find you, they sing…

18:24.394 --> 18:26.146
Hey! Are you okay?

18:27.314 --> 18:31.401
<i>This song inflicts debuff.</i>
<i>Are they monsters?</i>

18:31.944 --> 18:37.074
<i>Still, this Araba guy looks tough,</i>
<i>but he's been getting his ass kicked.</i>

18:38.117 --> 18:42.204
If we're against debuffers, then me
and my Contusion gotta deal with them.

18:44.581 --> 18:48.335
(Mermesis Berggren)

18:48.418 --> 18:49.711
I see.

18:49.795 --> 18:51.964
Those attractive looks.

18:52.047 --> 18:56.844
If I didn't know anything, I might
assume you're NPCs and lower my guard.

19:02.099 --> 19:03.559
Let me warn you-

19:03.642 --> 19:06.019
Man or woman,
no matter how good they look,

19:06.103 --> 19:08.689
I won't hesitate to kill
anyone who gets in my way.

19:10.065 --> 19:12.860
Your debuff won't work on me either.

19:12.943 --> 19:14.945
And flying in the air…

19:15.028 --> 19:17.948
…ain't gonna be an
advantage against me at all!

19:18.031 --> 19:20.742
Gravity Zero! Shana-oh Possession!

19:39.011 --> 19:40.387
Woohoo!

19:40.470 --> 19:43.056
A redo slash with Fleet Float!

19:43.140 --> 19:45.392
You let your guard down,
thinking you dodged me!

19:46.268 --> 19:48.395
Ouch!

19:48.478 --> 19:51.815
I took more damage than I expected.

19:53.650 --> 19:56.111
There's more chance of
accidents in air battles.

19:56.195 --> 19:58.363
Let's heal just in case.

20:02.784 --> 20:05.037
(Stamina not recovered)

20:06.371 --> 20:07.873
Damn it, I forgot!

20:07.956 --> 20:13.378
My Fool Arcanum makes healing items
have a chance of failing at me!

20:15.672 --> 20:19.176
Oh well, I'll go on without healing!

20:23.555 --> 20:25.390
Huh? Araba?!

20:31.438 --> 20:33.690
Bring it on, you damn fish!

20:33.774 --> 20:37.903
If you wish to have these
teeth rip you apart, that is!

20:42.407 --> 20:45.369
Hmph, in the end, they're just fish.

20:45.452 --> 20:49.456
You fight pretty wild, huh.
You ain't so bad after all.

20:50.540 --> 20:54.836
And the way you went airborne.
You <i>are</i> a Birdian, aren't you?

20:54.920 --> 20:56.964
Just give it up already!

20:57.047 --> 21:01.009
To tell the truth, I lost my
<i>arm</i> somewhere in this city.

21:01.093 --> 21:04.972
What you just saw was my
secret last resort, so to speak.

21:05.055 --> 21:08.350
Did you see a sword around
this size in your travels?

21:08.433 --> 21:12.562
It's a fine piece forged by
a master dwarven craftsman.

21:12.646 --> 21:14.648
No, I didn't.

21:14.731 --> 21:15.941
I see…

21:17.567 --> 21:21.113
I got chased by that fishman horde the
moment I came to this seabed city, after all.

21:21.196 --> 21:22.698
Seabed city?

21:22.781 --> 21:23.615
Hm?

21:23.699 --> 21:27.911
I see. If you've only just arrived,
you wouldn't know.

21:27.995 --> 21:29.037
Huh?

21:30.831 --> 21:34.418
What you see above us
isn't a stone ceiling.

21:34.501 --> 21:36.837
It's the bottom of the sea.

21:36.920 --> 21:37.754
Hm?

21:37.838 --> 21:40.299
And below us.

21:41.466 --> 21:46.763
Below this is the sea surface,
and below that is the sky.

21:46.847 --> 21:50.517
Hang on. I'm not following you.

21:50.600 --> 21:54.104
The above is the bottom,
and the below is the sea surface?

21:55.397 --> 21:58.525
Here in the Abyssal Capital Ruluiath…

21:58.608 --> 22:04.364
The entire city is teeming with the
"Turning" power of the Master of the Abyss.

22:04.448 --> 22:05.907
Huh…

22:05.991 --> 22:07.326
We call it…

22:08.076 --> 22:10.037
The "turned over" city.

22:31.516 --> 22:34.019
I hide in my brain every day

22:34.102 --> 22:35.979
cause I'm running out of patience

22:36.646 --> 22:38.440
lost in distorted thoughts

22:38.523 --> 22:42.402
I can't help but hold my breath

22:42.486 --> 22:44.613
blurred mind, spinning in place

22:44.696 --> 22:46.823
I long to turn away from that scene
to close my eyes.

22:46.907 --> 22:48.075
I don't like what I'm seeing

22:48.158 --> 22:48.992
and it's a curse

22:49.076 --> 22:51.203
it's a thorn in my side

22:52.537 --> 22:54.706
Countless eyes and voices

22:54.790 --> 23:01.505
clapping and laughing,
with a nihilistic air

23:01.588 --> 23:03.673
I'm losing my mind

23:03.757 --> 23:06.218
Inside this scary little world

23:06.301 --> 23:11.098
life is gradually soaking up my dopamine

23:11.181 --> 23:12.557
but I can breathe

23:12.641 --> 23:14.184
I can feel like I matter

23:14.267 --> 23:16.228
in my twisted imagination

23:16.311 --> 23:18.730
cause realitYhurts

23:18.814 --> 23:23.568
I think I'd rather stay here

23:28.615 --> 23:33.495
I think I'd rather stay here
